				<TD align=Right width=20%>
					Tip:</TD><TD>Caster tech for wiz
				</TD>
			</TR>
			<TR>
				<TD align=Right valign=top>
					Submitted By:
				</TD>
				<TD><a href="mailto:doomhammr@hotmail.com">darka</A><BR>&nbsp;
				</TD>
			</TR>
			<TR>
				<TD colspan=2>ive come across to many wizards who dont have a clue what they are doing and im really quite dazzled how they got any levels...<BR>rule nr 1 if u chaincast u will get trained .<BR>rule 2 if u stand to close u will get trained.<BR>my teq is to always take out maximum range on the spells and never ever stand to close to another caster, if u see damage reports u are to close.<BR>use the spells that are most mana dmg efficient when u reach a new spell level ur new spells tend to taunt and cost to much not to mention the resist rate... im lev 30 and i still use my lev 24 ice spell most since its rarely resisted and very low mana..<BR>in a group of lets say 1 tank  1 healer of any kind and a wiz , let the tank do its job first.. let him whack it a bit before u start casting when u start casting dont chain let 6 to 8 sec pass between casts that way u will make good dmg and it wont train on u, if u get trained then the tank is useless since u has to chase it around.<BR>IF they attack u dont cast again right away and IF u have a tank DO NOT RUN stand still take a few whacs since the tank cannot taunt if ur running. do not use AE spells <BR>if it can be avoided since the tend to make them all ur very best friend. AE in my oppinion is for decimating Greens.. <BR>This is not law and only my tech i use it and i havent gotten trained at all for 10 levels now and im gnerally liked in groups..(for my casting, my personality fucks it up sometimes)<BR>I suggest u try this tip and i promise u will level faster<BR><BR>Regards Darka Graverobber <BR>Wizard officer of <BR>Tornado Of Souls
				</TD>
			</TR>
		</table>

